  "finalReply": "Fixed run-length sweep stride bug in `ocaml/runtime/shared_heap.c` (`pool_sweep`).\n\n**Root cause:** pools are divided into fixed-size slots of `wh = wsize_sizeclass[sz]` words. Free runs are run-length encoded (`Wosize = blocks-1`), so iteration must advance by `wh` per slot, with an extra `wh * Wosize_hd(hd)` skip for free runs — as done correctly in `calc_pool_stats`, `pool_finalise`, `verify_pool`, and compaction. `pool_sweep` instead did `p += Whsize_hd(hd)` (object header size in words), so for any object smaller than its slot it landed mid-slot, misinterpreted payload as a header, corrupted the freelist/pool links, and crashed during bootstrap.\n\n**Fix (1 line):**\n```c\n-      p += Whsize_hd(hd);\n+      p += wh;\n```\n\n**Verification:**\n- `./configure` + `make -j` now completes (previously bootstrap compiler crashed); `ocamlc`/`ocamlopt` built.\n- `make -C testsuite one DIR=tests/basic`: 40 passed, 0 failed.",
  "error": null
